## Language & Runtime

### TypeScript v5.7.3

**Best Practices:**

- Enable strict mode in tsconfig.json
- Use explicit types, avoid `any` unless absolutely necessary
- Leverage advanced types: unions, intersections, generics
- Use `satisfies` operator for type checking without widening
- Enable `strictNullChecks` and `noImplicitAny`

**Version Notes:**

- TypeScript 5.7 includes improved type inference
- Better support for decorators (used extensively in NestJS)
- Enhanced performance for large codebases

### Node.js

**Required Version:** 18.x or higher (recommended: 20.x LTS)

**Best Practices:**

- Use LTS versions for production
- Leverage native fetch API (available in Node 18+)
- Use native test runner for simple tests (or Jest for complex scenarios)

## Database

### PostgreSQL (via pg driver v8.16.3)

**Components:**

- `pg`: ^8.16.3
- `@types/pg`: ^8.15.5 (dev)

**Best Practices:**

- Use connection pooling (implemented in DatabaseService)
- Always use parameterized queries to prevent SQL injection
- Implement Row-Level Security (RLS) for multi-tenancy
- Use transactions for multi-step operations
- Set appropriate pool size based on load (default: 20)
- Use prepared statements for frequently executed queries

**Version Notes:**

- pg v8.16.3 is stable and production-ready
- Native driver (no ORM overhead)
- Excellent TypeScript support with @types/pg
- Supports PostgreSQL 12+ features

**Architecture:**

- Custom repository pattern (no Prisma/TypeORM)
- BaseRepository for common CRUD operations
- Explicit column selection for performance
- Manual row mapping for type safety

## Authentication & Security

### Passport JWT v4.0.1

**Components:**

- `@nestjs/passport`: ^11.0.5
- `@nestjs/jwt`: ^11.0.1
- `passport`: ^0.7.0
- `passport-jwt`: ^4.0.1
- `@types/passport-jwt`: ^4.0.1 (dev)

**Best Practices:**

- Use separate strategies for identity tokens and tenant tokens
- Implement refresh token rotation
- Set appropriate JWT expiration times (access: 15m, refresh: 7d)
- Store refresh tokens securely in database
- Use HTTP-only cookies for web clients
- Implement token blacklisting for logout

**Version Notes:**

- Passport v0.7.0 is the latest with async/await support
- @nestjs/jwt v11 includes improved signing options
- Compatible with NestJS 11 dependency injection

### Bcrypt v6.0.0

**Components:**

- `bcrypt`: ^6.0.0
- `@types/bcrypt`: ^6.0.0

**Best Practices:**

- Use salt rounds of 10-12 for password hashing
- Never store plain text passwords
- Hash passwords before database insertion
- Use async methods (bcrypt.hash, bcrypt.compare) to avoid blocking

**Version Notes:**

- Bcrypt v6 includes performance improvements
- Native bindings for better performance
- Automatic salt generation

